1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,379
If your giant
predator eats

2
00:00:01,399 --> 00:00:02,779
everything,
why hasn't

3
00:00:02,799 --> 00:00:04,523
everything gone
extinct?

4
00:00:04,543 --> 00:00:05,366
Let's test it.

5
00:00:05,386 --> 00:00:06,416
This is the Grimmaw.

6
00:00:06,436 --> 00:00:08,114
It eats anything
that moves.

7
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:09,123
Press run.

8
00:00:09,143 --> 00:00:11,061
Year one:
mossbacks everywhere.

9
00:00:11,081 --> 00:00:12,236
Year three:
thinning.

10
00:00:12,256 --> 00:00:13,695
Year five:
gone.

11
00:00:13,715 --> 00:00:15,518
With nothing to hunt,
the Grimmaw starves

12
00:00:15,538 --> 00:00:16,207
too.

13
00:00:16,227 --> 00:00:18,020
A monster that eats
everything doesn't

14
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,045
rule your world.

15
00:00:19,065 --> 00:00:20,330
It ends it.

16
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:22,288
Real predators live
inside limits.

17
00:00:22,308 --> 00:00:23,325
Four are easy.

18
00:00:23,345 --> 00:00:24,939
The fifth is the
twist.

19
00:00:24,959 --> 00:00:26,057
One:
prey that breeds

20
00:00:26,077 --> 00:00:27,277
faster than it's
eaten.

21
00:00:27,297 --> 00:00:28,465
Two:
territory.

22
00:00:28,485 --> 00:00:30,237
One Grimmaw needs a
whole valley.

23
00:00:30,257 --> 00:00:31,349
Three:
energy.

24
00:00:31,369 --> 00:00:32,899
A body this big
hunts rarely and

25
00:00:32,919 --> 00:00:33,889
sleeps a lot.

26
00:00:33,909 --> 00:00:35,276
Four:
slow breeding.

27
00:00:35,296 --> 00:00:37,244
One cub every few
winters.

28
00:00:37,264 --> 00:00:38,231
Run it again.

29
00:00:38,251 --> 00:00:39,856
Now the numbers rise
and fall,

30
00:00:39,876 --> 00:00:41,464
but nothing vanishes.

31
00:00:41,484 --> 00:00:42,186
Rule five?

32
00:00:42,206 --> 00:00:43,474
Delete the monster.

33
00:00:43,494 --> 00:00:45,147
The mossbacks boom,
strip the meadow

34
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,593
bare,
then starve.

35
00:00:46,613 --> 00:00:48,243
Rule five is its job.

36
00:00:48,263 --> 00:00:50,369
The Grimmaw holds
the island together.

37
00:00:50,389 --> 00:00:51,692
Don't design a
monster.

38
00:00:51,712 --> 00:00:53,522
Design its place in
the world.

39
00:00:53,542 --> 00:00:55,246
Send this to a
monster designer.

40
00:00:55,266 --> 00:00:56,960
Part 26 of 50.

41
00:00:56,980 --> 00:01:00,348
Follow for part 27:
a dragon lands here.
